                <pb facs="0797" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1418: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-22T12:00:00+08:00">November 22,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 22—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>565. Following telegram has been sent to Shanghai: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 22, noon. Your 604, November 21, 4 p.m. I agree with your views
                            in this matter and approve action you and British Consul General propose
                            to take. I believe also that secrecy should be combated.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
